# 🧩 Puzzle Overhaul & Engagement Implementation Plan

This plan details the technical steps to transform the puzzle experience into a robust, addictive, and child-friendly learning environment with real-world data and rich UI feedback.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Lichess API Dependency**: The app will now require an internet connection for the latest daily puzzles (with local fallback).
> - **Vibration Permission**: On Android/iOS, the app will request vibration permissions for the "Wrong Move" feedback.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Data Layer & Service Refactor
#### [MODIFY] [puzzle_model.dart](file:///d:/PP942920DRIVE/PROJECTS/chess/app/lib/data/models/puzzle_model.dart)
- Update [Puzzle](file:///d:/PP942920DRIVE/PROJECTS/chess/app/lib/data/models/puzzle_model.dart#3-23) to include `rating`, `themes`, and `initialMove` (Lichess often starts a puzzle after an opponent move).
- Ensure [PuzzleMove](file:///d:/PP942920DRIVE/PROJECTS/chess/app/lib/data/models/puzzle_model.dart#24-40) supports UCI format directly for easier engine matching.

#### [MODIFY] [puzzle_repository.dart](file:///d:/PP942920DRIVE/PROJECTS/chess/app/lib/data/repositories/puzzle_repository.dart)
- Implement [getDailyPuzzle()](file:///d:/PP942920DRIVE/PROJECTS/chess/app/lib/data/repositories/puzzle_repository.dart#4-35) using `Dio` to fetch from `https://lichess.org/api/puzzle/daily`.
- Implement `getRandomPuzzle()` for **Puzzle Rush** and **Streak** modes.
- Add a local JSON fallback to ensure puzzles work offline.

---

### 2. Game Logic & Engagement (BLoC)
#### [MODIFY] [game_bloc.dart](file:///d:/PP942920DRIVE/PROJECTS/chess/app/lib/presentation/blocs/game/game_bloc.dart)
- **Puzzle Rush Mode**:
    - Add `rushTimer`, `rushStrikes` (max 3), and `rushScore` to [GameState](file:///d:/PP942920DRIVE/PROJECTS/chess/app/lib/presentation/blocs/game/game_bloc.dart#92-333).
    - Handle ticking timer and game-over conditions when strikes reach 3 or time hits zero.
- **Puzzle Streak**:
    - Track `streakCount` and `solveTime`.
    - Calculate XP: `baseXP (100) + speedBonus + difficultyMultiplier`.
- **AI Explanation**:
    - Add a `getPuzzleExplanation()` method that uses Stockfish/Sunfish to evaluate the position before and after the correct move to describe the tactical benefit (e.g., "This move forks the king and queen!").

---

### 3. UI/UX "Juiciness" & Feedback
#### [MODIFY] [game_screen.dart](file:///d:/PP942920DRIVE/PROJECTS/chess/app/lib/presentation/screens/game/game_screen.dart)
- **Visual Feedback**:
    - **Highlight Correct Move**: Draw a subtle green glow/overlay on the target square.
    - **Glow Effect**: Use `flutter_animate` to make the piece "pulse" when correctly placed.
    - **Fireworks**: Trigger a `ConfettiController` with a fireworks-style burst on puzzle completion.
- **Haptic & Sound**:
    - **Vibration**: Trigger `Vibration.vibrate()` on incorrect moves.
    - **Sounds**: Integrate `audioplayers` to play Chess.com style sounds (move, capture, correct, wrong).
- **Communication**:
    - **Child-Friendly Messages**: Map tactical terms to simpler language (e.g., "Double Attack" → "Super Sneaky Double Move!").

---

### 4. Aggregation
- Link `totalPuzzleXp` to the user's global profile XP.
- Persist `maxPuzzlesSolvedInDay` in [UserModel](file:///d:/PP942920DRIVE/PROJECTS/chess/app/lib/data/models/user_model.dart#3-107).

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- `flutter test` for [PuzzleRepository](file:///d:/PP942920DRIVE/PROJECTS/chess/app/lib/data/repositories/puzzle_repository.dart#3-36) mapping logic.
- Mock Lichess API responses to verify fallback behavior.

### Manual Verification
- **Puzzle Rush**: Verify timer countdown and strike accumulation.
- **Vibration**: Test on physical device (Android/iOS) to ensure haptics trigger on error.
- **Fireworks**: Finish a puzzle and confirm visual celebration.
- **AI Advisor**: Request an explanation and verify it accurately describes the win (e.g., "Wins a Knight").
